    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`; the generated `OwnersApi` interface declares the route (`@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` + `/owners`).\n\n## 0. Security gate (before anything)\n- `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must be an owner-admin, else 403.\n\n## 1. Framework validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (runs before the method body)\n\n**A. Bean Validation constraints on the DTO:**\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n- `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n- `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`; `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n- `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n- `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (cascade)\n- `title` constrained to enum MR/MRS/MS/DR\n\n**B. Three custom Spring `Validator`s wired via `@InitBinder` (errors join the same 400 response):**\n1. `OwnerFieldsValidator` \u2014 rejects blank firstName/lastName/city/telephone, and requires an address (structured `addressLine1` **or** flat `address`).\n2. `PostcodeValidator` \u2014 if postcode present, rejects if it doesn't match the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown cities accept any).\n3. `DisposableEmailDomainValidator` \u2014 rejects emails whose domain is on the disposable-domain list.\n\nAny failure here \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## 2. Method-body steps, in exact execution order\n1. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 `replayIdempotentCreate(Idempotency-Key)`: if the key was used before and the owner still exists, return that owner with **200** and stop (no new create).\n2. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, ignoring server-managed fields).\n3. **Resolve/normalize address** in place (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE; prefers structured over flat).\n4. **`registrationDateValidator.validate`** \u2014 throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400** if the date is in the future (null allowed).\n5. **Default registration date** to `LocalDate.now()` if null.\n6. **`businessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay`** \u2014 roll weekends/2026 holidays forward to next business day.\n7. **`telephoneNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 strip separators, apply `+61` default (drop leading 0), enforce E.164 national length; throws `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400** on failure.\n8. **`emailNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 blank\u2192null, else trim + lower-case.\n9. **`dailyRegistrationLimitValidator.validate`** \u2014 throws `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429** if \u2265100 owners already registered on that date.\n10. **`cityCapacityValidator.validate`** \u2014 throws `CityCapacityExceededException` \u2192 **409** if \u226550 owners already in that city.\n11. **Set `householdId`** = first 12 hex of `SHA-256(V2|lastName|postcode)`.\n12. **`duplicateIdentityValidator.validate`** \u2014 throws `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409** if a non-deleted owner shares identity key `SHA-256(V2|telephone|email|soundex(lastName))`.\n13. **Soft-duplicate handling** \u2014 if `sharesHousehold == true`, set `possibleDuplicate = false`; otherwise `possibleDuplicateDetector.detect` flags the earliest matching owner (same postcode + last-name Soundex, different identity). Never blocks.\n\n## 3. Persistence (`clinicService.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`)\n14. For a new owner without a `memberId`: generate `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><LuhnCheck>`) then de-duplicate against all existing member IDs (appending `-n`).\n15. For a new owner without a `namesakeCount`: compute count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n16. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 the actual DB insert.\n\n## 4. Post-save side-effects (still within the request)\n17. **`ownerAuditLogger.logCreated`** \u2014 writes two AUDIT log lines (human-readable + JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` with a sequence number).\n18. **`welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome`** \u2014 writes one NOTIFY log line.\n19. **`ownerIdempotencyStore.record`** \u2014 store Idempotency-Key \u2192 owner id (first write wins).\n20. **Map to `OwnerDto`** (computes derived read-only response fields), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes\n- There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`) and **no** application-event publishing \u2014 every side-effect above is an explicit call in the controller/service.\n- The `Owner`/`Person` entities also carry `@NotEmpty`/`@Email`/`@Pattern` annotations, but these are not actively enforced in this path since the entity is never re-validated after mapping (validation is on the DTO).\n- Idempotency store, audit, and notifier are all in-memory / log-only, not database writes."
